  '<p class="gd-p">Home tells you what to do next. Each car has its own page with its status, terms, bookings, invoices and photos.</p><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-home-at-a-glance" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Home at a glance</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The menu: Home, Vehicles, Bookings, Money (invoices, statements and payouts), Documents and Account (profile, banking and notifications).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">At the top: each car with its photo and its status right now (On rent, Available or In service), this month&#39;s rental charges against last month, the next payout and the days rented this month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Your earnings: a column per month. Press a month, or the arrows, for its bookings, days rented, rental charges, fees billed and the payout on its statement. Choose a car to see it alone, or <b class="gd-ui">Payouts</b> for the statement amounts. Beside it, Money (what is due now, your fees each month, the next billing date and the next payout date) and Coming up, your next bookings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Your vehicles: each car with this month so far, its next booking and what it needs next. Got another car? Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a vehicle</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1270"><img src="/guides/img/owner-01-home-desktop-9035b084.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1270"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.1%;top:8.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.9%;top:30.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:31.2%;top:85%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>When something needs you (a signature, a payment or an upload), it is the first thing on Home.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-a-car-s-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car&#39;s page</h2><p class="gd-p">Open Vehicles, then a car.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The top shows the car&#39;s photo, its plate, how it is enrolled and its status right now.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Terms: the Insurance Fee, the Revenue Share, your enrolment date and a link to the listing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">This car by month (choose a month with the arrows or its column), Coming up, and Bookings with every trip in your car. <b class="gd-ui">Book it for myself</b> reserves it for you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Leaving explains the exit notice and has the button to give it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/vehicles/1f21c3e5-39c3-4d54-ae0d-cbb2512835e7</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1242"><img src="/guides/img/owner-03-vehicle-desktop-7f1a9a38.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1242"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:55.6%;top:25.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:83.3%;top:38%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:36.5%;top:54.5%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:81.2%;top:67%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">While a car is being set up, its page also shows the onboarding checklist and the uploads it still needs: the ownership permit, the lender&#39;s permission and the insurance.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-service-and-maintenance" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Service and maintenance</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, under Service and maintenance.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>What is due on your car (oil change, tires, brakes, inspections, the registration) and the tires on it.</li><li>Every service we recorded: the date, the odometer, the shop, what was done and who paid.</li><li>You pay for maintenance and routine wear (your agreement, 11.1). A service we paid for shows its amount and is deducted on your next statement as an owner cost.</li><li>It is read only: call or message us about a service.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-take-new-listing-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Take new listing photos</h2><p class="gd-p">Good photos get more bookings. You can shoot them yourself with your phone.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the car&#39;s page, press <b class="gd-ui">Add listing photos</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Take new photos</b> for a car already live).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Read the tips for each shot: daylight, a plain background, the phone held landscape.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take photo</b> for each shot in the list. Press <b class="gd-ui">Retake</b> if one is not right.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The bar shows how many required photos you have.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Submit for listing</b>. New photos replace the current ones once our team approves them.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/610"><img src="/guides/img/field-06-photo-shoot-capture-phone-d0b13740.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="610"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:92.3%;top:43.4%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.9%;top:70.2%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('owner', 'fees-payments-and-payouts', 'chapter', 'bookings-and-your-own-use', 'Your fees are debited from your bank account on the 15th, after a notice. Your payout for the month before arrives on the 10th, with a statement.

## How your fees work

- Each car has two monthly fees: an insurance fee and a tracker fee. They are due every month, rented or not.
- The tracker fee starts the day the car''s tracker is installed. The tracker install fee has its own invoice.
- Before a car goes live you pay the first and last month amount we agreed with you (usually two months of the insurance fee, or the exact amount we agreed).
- Your amounts are the ones we agreed for each car, to the cent. Any other fee we agreed, for example a registration fee, comes on its own invoice with each line, its quantity and whether HST applies.
- Vehicles shows each car''s terms: the insurance fee and tracker fee a month and the Revenue Share, since when they apply, and any change coming. Open a car for its History: every period of terms and every notice we sent (Download the notice).
- Lower amounts apply from the date in our notice. A higher fee comes with 30 days'' written notice; a higher Revenue Share applies only if you sign an updated Vehicle Schedule. A month whose fee changes part way is billed per day at each amount.
- One invoice per car. Registry, inspection and appraisal costs are not billed by us unless we agreed to pay them for you; then they are on an invoice of their own.

An invoice we cancel shows Void with the reason, and the invoice that replaces it. Nothing is debited for a void invoice. Every invoice has Download PDF.

## The monthly debit, step by step

:::flow
Notice day | 10 days before: your invoices and one email with the total
The 15th | Each invoice is debited from your account
Cleared | The invoice shows Paid and you get a receipt
Insufficient funds? | A $50.00 Late Fee once, and the same amount tried again within 30 days
:::

- A debit is never more than its notice said. Each invoice shows "will be debited on" with the date.
- If your bank returns a debit for insufficient funds, we add the $50.00 Late Fee to that invoice once and try the original amount again within 30 days, as section 4.4 of your Enrollment Agreement sets out. The Late Fee is collected with your next debit.
- Returned for another reason (for example a closed account)? We do not try again and add no Late Fee. We pause your debit and email you: pay the invoice from its page, or set up a new account under Account > Banking.
- Returned again after the retry? The invoice is in arrears and we contact you.
- You can always pay an invoice by card from its page before the debit day.
- On your bank statement the debit shows our company''s legal name, operating as CarmaCars.

## Set up the automatic debit

Do this once. Without it, we email you on each notice day to set it up.

1. Open **Account** > **Banking**. Under Automatic debit of your fees, press **Set up pre-authorized debit**.
2. Read the agreement and press **Continue to my bank details**.
3. Enter your bank details and press **Save the bank account**. Banking then shows the account and the next debit.

![](/guides/img/owner-07-banking-desktop-52316739.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 752; address: carmacars.ca/owner/banking; pins: 1 96.2 36.8")

## Pay an invoice now

1. Open Invoices, then the invoice. It lists what it covers and the balance.
2. Choose Card (paid at once) and press **Pay $...**.
3. Or choose Pre-authorized debit (from a Canadian bank account, clears in 3 to 5 business days) and press **Authorize debit of $...**.
4. Prefer Interac e-Transfer? Send the amount to billing@carmacars.ca with the invoice number in the message.

![](/guides/img/owner-06-invoice-desktop-bba2c020.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 742; address: carmacars.ca/owner/invoices/INV-1050; pins: 2 6.9 52.6, 3 38.2 52.6, 4 11.5 80.5")

> Tip: Paid us by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer? Once we record it, the invoice says "Paid by e-Transfer on" the date, you get a receipt by email, and the automatic debit does not take that amount. Paid part of it? The invoice shows Partly paid and only the rest is debited.

## Tell us where to pay you

1. Open **Account** > **Banking**. Under Where we pay you, choose Bank transfer or e-Transfer.
2. Fill in Account holder, Institution number, Transit number and Account number (or your e-Transfer email).
3. Press **Submit payout details**. For your security we confirm new details by phone before we use them.

![](/guides/img/owner-07-banking-desktop-87b2ffe3.jpg "desktop; size: 990 642; address: carmacars.ca/owner/banking; pins: 1 50.5 25.7, 2 90.9 45.5, 3 30.3 89.7")

## Statements and payouts

1. This month so far, at the top of Statements: the rentals finished this month, your Owner Revenue, the Revenue Share, fees and deductions and the expected payout, worked out live and marked Provisional. Rentals still under way are listed below it.
2. Statements: one a month, once approved by CarmaCars; the approved statement is the final one. Open one to see every booking, the revenue share, deductions and the payout.
3. Press **Download PDF** to keep a copy. We also email it to you with the PDF attached.
4. Payouts shows what was paid to you and when. Payouts are made on the 10th for the month before.

![](/guides/img/owner-09-statement-desktop-fc5f9ea5.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 792; address: carmacars.ca/owner/statements/f27936a8-9bfb-4280-81ae-c67ec47febe1; pins: 2 16.0 30.6, 1 66.0 40.9")
