/div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Enter your bank details and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the bank account</b>. Banking then shows the account and the next debit.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/banking</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/752"><img src="/guides/img/owner-07-banking-desktop-52316739.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="752"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:96.2%;top:36.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fees-payments-and-payouts-pay-an-invoice-now" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pay an invoice now</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open Invoices, then the invoice. It lists what it covers and the balance.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose Card (paid at once) and press <b class="gd-ui">Pay $...</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Or choose Pre-authorized debit (from a Canadian bank account, clears in 3 to 5 business days) and press <b class="gd-ui">Authorize debit of $...</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Prefer Interac e-Transfer? Send the amount to billing@carmacars.ca with the invoice number in the message.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/invoices/INV-1050</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/742"><img src="/guides/img/owner-06-invoice-desktop-bba2c020.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="742"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:6.9%;top:52.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:38.2%;top:52.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:11.5%;top:80.5%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Paid us by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer? Once we record it, the invoice says &quot;Paid by e-Transfer on&quot; the date, you get a receipt by email, and the automatic debit does not take that amount. Paid part of it? The invoice shows Partly paid and only the rest is debited.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fees-payments-and-payouts-tell-us-where-to-pay-you" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tell us where to pay you</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Banking</b>. Under Where we pay you, choose Bank transfer or e-Transfer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Fill in Account holder, Institution number, Transit number and Account number (or your e-Transfer email).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Submit payout details</b>. For your security we confirm new details by phone before we use them.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/banking</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:990/642"><img src="/guides/img/owner-07-banking-desktop-87b2ffe3.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="990" height="642"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50.5%;top:25.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:90.9%;top:45.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:30.3%;top:89.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fees-payments-and-payouts-statements-and-payouts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Statements and payouts</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">This month so far, at the top of Statements: the rentals finished this month, your Owner Revenue, the Revenue Share, fees and deductions and the expected payout, worked out live and marked Provisional. Rentals still under way are listed below it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Statements: one a month, once approved by CarmaCars; the approved statement is the final one. Open one to see every booking, the revenue share, deductions and the payout.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Download PDF</b> to keep a copy. We also email it to you with the PDF attached.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Payouts shows what was paid to you and when. Payouts are made on the 10th for the month before.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/statements/380cc1bb-bfd5-4e55-8022-93a3b998ca74</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/792"><img src="/guides/img/owner-09-statement-desktop-fc5f9ea5.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="792"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:16%;top:30.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:66%;top:40.9%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('owner', 'documents-and-forms', 'chapter', 'fees-payments-and-payouts', 'Your signed agreements, uploads and government forms are under Documents. Some forms are filled for you; Forms C and D are signed with witnesses.

## Sign everything at once

Everything you sign on screen is in one place: Home shows how many are signed ("2 of 5 signed") and opens it with Check and sign.

1. Press **Check and sign** on Home (or open `carmacars.ca/owner/sign`). The list at the top shows each document: signed, in this package, or done elsewhere (Forms C and D, the bank debit).
2. Check the key values: your name, address, each car with its VIN and plate, your fees and Revenue Share. Something wrong? Press **Fix** next to it, change it, and come back.
3. Open any document to read it word for word: the agreements, the schedules and Forms A and B. The official registry forms are not in it: they are printed and signed in ink.
4. Tap **All of these** for the statements the agreement asks you to initial (your initials are filled in), then press **Sign all**.
5. Your name on file is your signature. One signature is applied to each document; CarmaCars countersigns at the same moment and every signed copy is in Documents.

> Two owners: A car with a second owner on its ownership? Each owner named in the Title Schedule signs. The other owner gets their own link by email and signs the same documents on their phone or computer. The agreements take effect when the last owner signs; CarmaCars countersigns then.

> Good to know: Form A (the trust declaration) is for cars under the Co-Registrant or Transfer method; Form B (the lease summary) for cars under a Lease method. No witness is needed: they are in the same package. You can also sign one on its own page from Documents.

> Tip: Signed one of your documents on paper instead? Send us the scan. Once we record it, Documents shows it as Signed on paper and we do not ask again.

## We set up your car for you

When our team enters your car for you, you get one email: review the details and sign.

1. No sign-in yet? The email has a link to choose your password. It works once, for 24 hours; after that use Forgot password on the sign-in page.
2. Open `carmacars.ca/owner/review` (Home has **Review or correct your details**). Check your phone and address, and each car: plate, colour, odometer, your insurer and your lender. The terms we agreed are shown too.
3. Something wrong? Correct it and press **Save corrections**. Your documents are filled in again and we are told. A term you did not agree to: message us before you sign.
4. Everything right? Press **Everything is right: sign** and sign once.

## Sign an updated Vehicle Schedule

When we agree new terms for a car you already signed for, you sign an updated Vehicle Schedule. Home shows it first.

1. Open it from Home or the email. It shows what changes (now and updated) and the date it applies from.
2. Read the text, tick that you agree, type your full legal name and press **Sign**.
3. Your current terms stay until you sign. After that, your invoices and statements use the new ones from the date.

## Form C on screen, with your witness beside you

Form C is the lender or lessor permission for a financed or leased car. It needs one witness, and you can sign it on screen when your witness is with you.

1. Open Documents. Under Forms to sign with witnesses, press Sign Form C on screen instead.
2. Initial each of the three acknowledgments, and type Your initials.
3. Sign: draw your signature in the box, or use your name.
4. Hand the device to your witness, another adult. They type their full name and tick the statement "I witnessed (your name) sign in my presence." Press **Sign Form C**.

![](/guides/img/owner-16-form-c-screen-desktop-faa92983.jpg "desktop; size: 790 980; address: carmacars.ca/owner/documents/form-c/b39a2a4e-6dcb-459c-b7c0-393f78919d91; pins: 2 5.7 13.6, 3 32.9 55.1, 4 6.3 82.2")

## Forms C and D on paper, signed with witnesses

Form D is a limited power of attorney (two witnesses), signed on paper. Form C can be signed on paper too, with one witness.

1. Open Documents. Under Forms to sign with witnesses, press **Print the form**. It is filled in, and every spot to sign or initial is marked SIGN HERE or INITIAL HERE.
2. Sign it in front of your witnesses. They sign and print their names in their spots.
3. Type each witness''s full name in the boxes.
4. On your phone, press **Take a photo of the signed page**: one photo of each page. A PDF scan works too (**Or choose a file**).

![](/guides/img/owner-12-forms-c-d-desktop-21fbbe79.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 742; address: carmacars.ca/owner/documents; pins: 1 21.5 32.5, 3 69.4 50.7, 4 69.4 60.4")

> Tip: We check the photo and approve it, or send it back with what to fix. You get an email either way, and the page shows the status.

> Good to know: Why paper for Form D? It is a power of attorney, which cannot be signed electronically in Ontario, and its two witnesses sign in person.

## Government forms filled for you

Each car''s registry forms are prepared from your records. Until we load the official PDF, you get a data sheet with the values.

1. Open Documents and choose a form marked "Official form, filled for you".
2. Press **Download the filled form** and check each value.
3. Print it and sign it in ink. It is the official ServiceOntario form exactly as ServiceOntario publishes it, with only its empty text boxes filled in. Its boxes to tick and its signatures are done by hand, at the registry office or before you go, as we tell you.

![](/guides/img/owner-13-official-form-desktop-48614913.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 732; address: carmacars.ca/owner/documents/forms/7624af13-b86c-4add-a2e7-b11651149086/official; pins: 2 22.2 29.5")

> Good to know: ON00453 (a company''s registrant number) is an Adobe form: open it in Adobe Acrobat Reader (free) to see and print it. Other PDF viewers show a blank page, as they do with the form downloaded from ServiceOntario.

> Watch out: Official registry forms are never signed on screen. You pay ServiceOntario, the inspection station and the appraiser directly.
