1. **Hide from the owner** keeps the booking''s revenue from the owner until the car is returned, or until the owner statement covering it is approved. The owner sees the booking as Booked with its dates, and the calendar still shows the car busy. Add a reason if you like: it is kept in the history.
2. **Show to the owner** shows it now. Approving the statement shows every hidden booking on it by itself.
3. Not shown to the owner is for a booking with no owner revenue (an insurance placeholder, a shareholder''s or the owner''s own use at no charge): the owner sees only that the car is unavailable for those dates. A booking with revenue cannot be set this way.
4. Add a rental and Send an offer have What the owner sees. It starts from Settings > Program, Owners and fleet: Owners see a booking''s revenue (right away by default).
5. On the Money tab, Owner deductions on this booking: **Add a booking expense** (cleaning, repair, fuel, platform fee or other, the amount, the reason the owner reads, a receipt number) comes off before Owner Revenue.
6. **Set the Revenue Share for this booking** applies within the car''s signed terms. Above the terms only an Admin can, with Above the signed terms ticked and the reason. **Back to the car''s terms** undoes it.
7. Add a rental has the same under The car''s owner.

> Good to know: The owner''s statement always includes every booking at its true amounts and lists each deduction with its reason, so the payout is always right. Customer service and sales add deductions only while Program settings let them change fees.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">A booking starts as a request from the website, or as an offer you send yourself to a customer on the phone. You check it, adjust it and send the offer; an offer that is out is changed in place. After that, the booking page holds the money, documents, changes and history.</p><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-request-queue" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The request queue</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Requests</b>. The oldest waiting request is at the top.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by New, Waiting on the renter, Pushed back, Offer out, Signing and payment, or Offer expired.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Waiting shows how long the renter has waited; red means past the first reply target (5 minutes, set in Program settings). Open a booking number to answer it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/requests</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/820"><img src="/guides/img/admin-02-requests-desktop-6521282d.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="820"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:38.9%;top:29.9%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:22.2%;top:43.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A request whose pickup time passes without an offer expires by itself, with a note in its history. The renter is not emailed unless &quot;Email the renter when their request expires that way&quot; is on in Program settings.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-answer-a-request-with-an-offer" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Answer a request with an offer</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The Review and offer tab shows the request as the renter sent it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Adjust the car, the dates, the rate type, the places, the rates and fees, the deposit and extras.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Price on the right updates as you change things.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add a message, choose how long the offer stays open, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1200/1550"><img src="/guides/img/admin-03-booking-review-desktop-353f3707.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="1550"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:5%;top:6.5%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:7.5%;top:45.8%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.2%;top:42.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.7%;top:98.1%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol" start="5"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Changed fields but not ready to send? Press <b class="gd-ui">Save changes</b>. The panel &quot;The offer as the renter sees it&quot; shows the result.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Can&#39;t do it? Press <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> and fill in Reason and any alternative.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Need an answer first? Press <b class="gd-ui">Ask the renter</b> to send a question.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:500/80"><img src="/guides/img/admin-03-booking-review-desktop-4dd4ed06.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="500" height="80"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:41.2%;top:52.5%" aria-hidden="true">6</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18%;top:52.5%" aria-hidden="true">7</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-send-an-offer-without-a-request" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Send an offer without a request</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer</b> on Bookings and on Requests. For a customer on the phone, by text or at the counter: no request needed.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The customer: type a name, phone or email and choose them. Not on file? Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a new customer</b>: full legal name, mobile, email (the offer link goes there) and date of birth. A customer already on file with the same email or phone is shown with Use: one person, one record.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The car and the dates: type the car code, plate or name, or choose from the list; each car says Free or Not free for the dates. Then the pickup and return places (our location, delivery with the address and distance, airport).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The price: the Rate sheet, A total for the whole rental, or A rate per day (times the days). A price typed by hand needs its reason and can be plus tax or tax included. Set the kilometres, a promo code, the deposit, a discount and each fee (an Admin), and how damage is covered: with option 3 the Protection Plan price is the one the renter pays.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">How it is paid: the rental by card online (the usual way), e-Transfer, cash, cheque, bank transfer, platform payout or the insurer; the deposit by card hold, cash, e-Transfer or no deposit (an Admin).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Who found this client, the message to the renter, how long the offer is open, and how the link goes: Email, Text, both or neither.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">The right side is the offer as the renter will see it, priced by the database as you type. Press <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Save without sending</b> keeps it as a request for later.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>It makes the same request and offer the website makes: the renter approves, signs and pays (or you record the payment), and only then is the car on the calendar. No &quot;request received&quot; email goes to the renter for an offer you send. Staff commissions and statements count it like any other booking.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-change-an-offer-that-is-out" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change an offer that is out</h2><p class="gd-p">The renter has the offer (Offered), or approved it and has not paid (Signing and payment). Press <b class="gd-ui">Edit the offer</b> on the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Change anything: the car, the dates, the places, the price, fees, the deposit, add-ons, how it is paid. Each changed field is highlighted and the before and after are listed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Write what changed in Message to the renter and choose how long the offer is open.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save and send the update</b>: the renter gets the new version by email or text (ticked), and the old version no longer counts. Or press <b class="gd-ui">Save without telling the renter</b> and tell them yourself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A confirmed booking is changed with <b class="gd-ui">Change the booking</b> (Propose a change, below).</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>No need to withdraw first. <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw the offer</b> is only for taking it back for good; <b class="gd-ui">Send again, later expiry</b> gives the renter more time, and <b class="gd-ui">Renter approved by phone</b> records a yes given on a call.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-edit-a-booking-that-has-started" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Edit a booking that has started</h2><p class="gd-p">On a confirmed, on-trip or returned booking (an Admin: a closed one too), Overview, <b class="gd-ui">Edit the booking</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Change the pickup or the return (extend or shorten: the rental charge is worked out again at this booking&#39;s rates), the car (on trip: the car it leaves goes to Out of service for Fleet to check), the rental charge for the trip, each fee, the kilometres a day, the deposit (an Admin) and the note.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Type why, if you like, and tick <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter what changed</b>, or leave it off for a silent correction. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the changes</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">What is open now shows at once: <b class="gd-ui">Email a pay link</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Text a pay link</b> for exactly that amount, <b class="gd-ui">Charge</b> the saved card (the renter agreed), or record cash or an e-Transfer on the Money tab.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Each edit is kept with who, when, why, before and after (Edits, under the form) and in the booking&#39;s history. A closed booking&#39;s owner split and the staff commission follow. To have the renter accept and sign first, use Propose a change instead.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-fees-a-forgotten-fee-and-the-balance" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fees, a forgotten fee and the balance</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking&#39;s Money tab, Fees lists each fee. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change or add a fee</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type a new amount (for the whole trip, before HST) beside any fee, or choose one not on the booking (the young driver fee shows its price for these dates), or add a charge of its own with or without HST.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the fees</b>. The balance shows by part (rental, fees) with the pay link, the saved card and Record a payment beside it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The renter sees the balance on their booking with a Pay button, and pays by card on Stripe&#39;s form.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Every change is recorded (Changes to the fees): the amount before and after, who and why. Customer service and sales may change fees while Program settings, Staff may change fees, is on.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-correct-a-renter-s-details" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Correct a renter&#39;s details</h2><p class="gd-p">On the renter&#39;s page (People, Renters) or on any of their bookings, <b class="gd-ui">Edit renter</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Correct the name, email, phone, date of birth, licence, home address (start typing to find it) or the staff note.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A new email also becomes their sign-in at once (no confirmation needed for a typo you correct); tick <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter a link to set a password</b> to send one there. Unsigned agreements and offers go to the new address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the renter</b>. An email that another renter has is refused with their name; the same phone is a warning.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The same person entered twice? Possible duplicates (same email, same phone, or same name and date of birth) shows under the renter. <b class="gd-ui">Merge into this record</b> moves the other record&#39;s bookings, licences, cards, payments, documents and messages here and fills any detail missing here; the other record stays, blocked, with the merge in both histories.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-payments-by-part-the-rental-the-deposit-and-later-charges" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payments by part: the rental, the deposit and later charges</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking&#39;s Money tab, Money by part shows what is still open for the rental, the fees and later charges, the deposit and the card on file. Each part is paid its own way, in any mix: for example the deposit in cash and the rental by card.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Record a payment</b>: choose what it is for (the rental, fees, the deposit or a later charge) and how it was paid (e-Transfer, cash, cheque, bank transfer, platform payout, the insurer). An e-Transfer, cheque or transfer needs its reference. Press <b class="gd-ui">Record it</b>. The renter gets a receipt; <b class="gd-ui">Print</b> prints one to hand over.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Collect a card</b>: a payment (Everything open by default: the rental, the fees and any later charge in one), the deposit hold or saving the card. The renter types the card in Stripe&#39;s secure form: on this device (<b class="gd-ui">Open the card form</b>, then hand it over) or by a link texted or emailed to them (<b class="gd-ui">Send the link</b>). Staff never type a card number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A deposit hold lasts about 7 days and shows the days left; while the car is out it is collected by itself before it lapses. After the return, settle the deposit (below). <b class="gd-ui">Capture the hold</b> for all of it keeps the money; a part capture or <b class="gd-ui">Release the hold</b> waits for the settlement while the car is out or something is open (an Admin may do it with the reason).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge the saved card</b> (Finance or an Admin): extra kilometres, fuel, damage or a late return, with the reason the renter&#39;s receipt shows. For a rental over 7 days, save the card and charge the deposit this way.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">An offer paid another way: once the renter approved and signed and the money is recorded, the booking is confirmed (or press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm the booking</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A deposit taken in cash or by e-Transfer is given back the same way after the return: Finance gets a task; press <b class="gd-ui">Returned</b> with the reference or receipt number.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Statements, reconciliation and the deposit settlement read each payment with its method: a cash deposit is never refunded to a card.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-settle-the-deposit" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Settle the deposit</h2><p class="gd-p">The deposit is never given back by itself. Finance or an Admin settles it after the return: on the booking&#39;s Money tab, under Deposit, press <b class="gd-ui">Settle the deposit</b>. Issue the Check-in statement first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The form shows the deposit, what is still available, the charges owed from the statement and what is taken from the deposit for them. What the deposit does not cover is charged to the card on file; with no card (or a card declined), the renter gets a pay link by email and text, and Finance has a task until it is paid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Tolls and tickets can take up to 7 days to come in. Inside that window the whole rest of the deposit is filled in as the hold-back, until the window ends. To give it back sooner, tick Release now anyway: a toll that comes in later is charged to the card on file.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Something still open keeps the whole deposit: an incident, a claim, new damage at the return not priced, damage found later not billed, a toll or ticket on the car during the rental not matched or not charged, a card dispute, or charges not on a statement yet. The form lists them. Only an Admin can release part of it, with the reason; it is recorded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Damage: <b class="gd-ui">Keep the whole deposit (damage)</b> turns what is left of the deposit into a damage charge, with what was damaged and the photos; the renter is told. <b class="gd-ui">Bill damage</b> adds a damage charge up to the $2,500 deductible (more goes through a claim): the deposit pays first, then the card on file.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Settle</b>. The money moves at Stripe at once: the charges are collected and what is not owed is refunded or the hold released. A step Stripe refuses is tried again by itself, and Finance gets a task if it keeps failing.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A card hold lapses after about 7 days. While the car is out, or returned and not settled, the hold is collected in full a day and a half before it lapses: that keeps the money, and the settlement refunds what is not owed. A hold that lapses anyway is charged to the saved card, and Finance is told at once.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-a-booking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A booking</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b>, then a booking number. Or type the number in the search box.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Tabs: Overview, Money, Changes, History, and Drivers and documents.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Overview shows the trip, the renter, what is still missing for the handover, and the price.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open tasks for this booking, with the queue and the due time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Top right: <b class="gd-ui">Stop blocking the calendar</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Cancel for the renter</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Cancel by CarmaCars</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Under the booking number: where the booking is on its way, from Request to Closed, with the dates, the days, the total and who pays.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10065</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/960"><img src="/guides/img/admin-04-booking-desktop-b56b668a.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="960"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50%;top:46.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:85.4%;top:14.5%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:22.9%;top:26.8%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-check-a-car-out-or-in" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check a car out or in</h2><p class="gd-p">From the booking, with your phone or a tablet: the same checklist field staff use.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A confirmed booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Check out (pickup)</b> under Check-out, check-in and signing; a booking on rent shows <b class="gd-ui">Check in (return)</b>. Today lists the check-outs and check-ins due, each with <b class="gd-ui">Check out</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The checklist opens: the ready check, the renter and their licence and card, the odometer (km) and fuel or charge, the keys, the photo set (every side, the wheels, the interior, the odometer and fuel gauge, the plate), damage marks with close-ups, then the renter and you sign.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Photos wait on the device without a connection and upload in the background. Each keeps its time, and the place when the device allows location.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A field job of the booking is taken over (the history says so); with no job, one is made for you. When done, press <b class="gd-ui">See the photo report</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in the same way from their own booking page.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-photo-report-late-returns-and-the-return-charges" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The photo report, late returns and the return charges</h2><p class="gd-p">Under Check-out, check-in and signing, press <b class="gd-ui">Photo report</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The report shows the due-back time, the actual check-out and check-in, Late by (or Overdue by while the car is out), the odometer and kilometres over the allowance, the fuel or charge out and in, every photo with its time and place, and the damage.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">At check-in the late return (after the grace period of the fee defaults), the mileage overage and the fuel or recharging are written to the return charges at once. A gas car with no pump receipt is priced at the refill price per eighth (Program settings) plus the markup until the receipt is entered.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Not charging one? Press <b class="gd-ui">Waive</b> beside it and give the reason: it stays waived if the charges are worked out again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The time was wrong? Press <b class="gd-ui">Correct the check-in time</b> (or the check-out time) with the reason: lateness and the late charges follow, and the history keeps both times.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The renter gets the same report (without these buttons) by email and in their Documents. Late by shows on the booking and in the Bookings list.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-signatures-on-the-spot-or-by-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Signatures on the spot, or by link</h2><p class="gd-p">The renter or an additional driver signs the rental agreement on your device, or on their own phone.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">While a signature is missing, the booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Email the signing link</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text the signing link</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">No agreement made yet (the renter has not saved their details at home)? <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b> still shows: press <b class="gd-ui">Prepare the agreement to sign now</b> and it is made on the spot.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>: confirm the name matches their licence and that you saw the original licence (photograph it if none is on file), then press <b class="gd-ui">Hand the device to</b> and their name.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">They read both agreements (CarmaCars&#39; and Blind Spot&#39;s), tick the statements and sign. Then <b class="gd-ui">Back to the staff view</b> for the next signer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The record is the same as signing online, and says it was signed in person, collected by you, on your device. It is printed on the signed copy&#39;s signature record page.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-rental-agreements-every-version-every-field" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rental agreements: every version, every field</h2><p class="gd-p">The booking&#39;s Rental agreements card: the current version of CarmaCars&#39; and Blind Spot&#39;s agreements, every earlier one, and what is still blank.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Once the agreement is signed and countersigned, any change to what it prints makes a new version of both documents by itself: the dates, the price lines, the car, a driver added or corrected, the coverage, the deposit or how it was paid, an address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A change to the dates, the price, the car, the drivers or the coverage option is signed again: the renter (and each driver it affects) gets their link by email and text, and the card shows &quot;Agreement v3 waiting for signature&quot;. A correction (a typo in an address, a plate written differently) is filed without signing; the renter gets the corrected copy by email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check-out makes the &quot;as picked up&quot; copy (time out, km out, fuel out, the car&#39;s plate and VIN, the check-out report), countersigned by whoever checked the car out; check-in makes the closing copy (time in, km in, driven and charged, fuel in, late hours, damage, the return charges, the final totals). Both go to the renter by email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Every version</b> lists each one with what changed and both PDFs. <b class="gd-ui">Resend the signing links</b>, or press the button with their first name beside it to have them sign on your phone or tablet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The card lists what the agreements still print blank (a licence expiry, the insurer&#39;s policy number, the insured vehicle, a VIN). Type the values and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the missing fields</b>: the agreements follow.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Check-out stops while a field a claim needs is blank. An Admin can let it go ahead: type the reason and press <b class="gd-ui">Override</b>; the reason is in the booking&#39;s history.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Make the agreements again</b> checks both against the booking at once (they also follow every change by themselves).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-signing-that-holds-up-in-a-dispute" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Signing that holds up in a dispute</h2><p class="gd-p">Every signature of a rental agreement, an amendment or a new version is made the same way, remotely or on your device.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The signer confirms it is them with a 6-digit code sent to their phone or email on file; the licence on file is shown.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">They say they read the documents, initial the key terms (damage and the deductible, the deposit and later charges, fuel, kilometres and late returns, their coverage, cancellation), give three consents (to sign electronically, to receive records electronically, to card charges under the agreement) and draw their signature.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each step is recorded with its time, IP address and device, and the place when the device shares it. The signed PDFs end with a certificate of completion; anyone can check a signed file at <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/verify</span>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Typed names are off. For a signer who cannot draw, an Admin can turn on the accessibility fallback: <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, Esign typed fallback.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-card-disputes-the-evidence-pack" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Card disputes: the evidence pack</h2><p class="gd-p">Everything that proves the rental, in one PDF for Stripe.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">When a card payment is disputed, the evidence pack is built by itself: the signed agreements with their certificates, the check-out and check-in reports with photos, kilometres and fuel, the licence, the payments and charges, every message to the renter, and the card checks from Stripe. It is staged in Stripe as the dispute&#39;s evidence, and To do gets an urgent task.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open the booking: the Rental agreements card shows the pack. Press <b class="gd-ui">Download</b> to check it, then <b class="gd-ui">Submit to Stripe</b> before the evidence date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Build the dispute evidence pack</b> makes one at any time (an Admin or Finance).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-licence-before-an-offer-is-accepted" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The licence before an offer is accepted</h2><p class="gd-p">Front, back and a selfie, from the request on.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">After sending a request the renter is asked for their licence. A licence already on file from an earlier booking is used again while it is valid after the return.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The offer cannot be accepted (by the renter, or by you on their word) and nothing is paid until the licence and its expiry date are on file.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Review the images as usual with <b class="gd-ui">Review documents</b>: the card Renter documents is on Review and offer too.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The switch is in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, Booking requests and offers: Booking licence required (on), with the selfie (on).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-renter-documents-licence-and-proof-of-coverage" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Renter documents: licence and proof of coverage</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter&#39;s licence photos, selfie and proof of coverage (OPCF 27 or a credit card&#39;s rental coverage) are checked before the handover. You check them yourself; no task is needed.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A booking with documents waiting is a line on To do: &quot;Check &#39;s documents for booking &quot;, marked Now when the pickup is within two days. Press <b class="gd-ui">Review documents</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The pop-up shows each driver&#39;s images and the coverage: the insurer, policy number and expiry, or the card, its type and whether the name matches.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">What to check is written once at the top. One wrong? Open <b class="gd-ui">Reject this one</b> under it, type the reason the renter reads and press <b class="gd-ui">Reject</b>: they are asked for a new one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Then press <b class="gd-ui">Approve all</b>: every image, the proof of coverage and the Protection Plan still waiting are approved in one step. Anything the system refuses is named with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The same pop-up is on the booking: the card Renter documents (<b class="gd-ui">Review documents</b>) on Overview and on Drivers and documents.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Each opening of a renter&#39;s documents is logged. The links to the images last one minute. Field staff can also check a licence in person at the check-out (photos and four checks): the history says &quot;checked in person&quot;. Field staff also review the licence images (not the coverage) of bookings on their own jobs in the next 7 days from My jobs, with the same Approve all or a reason to reject: the history says the reviewer&#39;s role, field.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-payments-by-day" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payments by day</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Payments by day</b>: every payment and refund of a day or a range, by method, the cash drawer and the refunds waiting. Finance has the same screen.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose From and To and the methods (card, e-Transfer, cash, cheque, platform payout, insurer, bank transfer, pre-authorized debit, other), then press <b class="gd-ui">Show</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Totals by method and for each day; cards read as the card and its last four digits, never a code.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The cash drawer: expected (cash in less cash given back) against the count Finance records with <b class="gd-ui">Record the count</b>; a difference shows over or short.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Refunds waiting: every refund asked for anywhere with the policy maths. <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with the reason in the row, then <b class="gd-ui">Issue the refund</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Export CSV</b> for the bookkeeper.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-propose-a-change-to-a-confirmed-booking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Propose a change to a confirmed booking</h2><p class="gd-p">The renter gets an email and answers on their booking. The calendar moves only when they accept.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the booking&#39;s Changes tab. Under Propose a change, set the new pickup, return or car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">To price it by hand, type a New rental charge before tax. Leave it empty to use the car&#39;s rates.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Write the Reason, for the renter. They read it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Preview the price</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Send to the renter</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10065?tab=changes</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1200/520"><img src="/guides/img/admin-05-booking-changes-desktop-97008b21.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="520"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:17.5%;top:33.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:9.2%;top:50%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:38.3%;top:71.2%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:12.9%;top:91.9%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-who-a-booking-is-credited-to" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Who a booking is credited to</h2><p class="gd-p">Overview (and Review and offer) shows the Sales credit: the staff member the booking counts for in their sales.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A quote or a rental is credited to whoever created or added it. A request from the website is credited to whoever sent its first offer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">To give it to someone else, press <b class="gd-ui">Reassign</b>, choose who (or Nobody), say whether they sourced the client and write the reason. The booking&#39;s history and the audit log keep it, and the deal stays in the same week and month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Sourced means the staff member chose I sourced this client when they entered it, it came with a field staff referral link, or you credited it. Only a sourced booking earns a staff commission. A website request earns none unless you credit someone.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Someone said they sourced a website request? The credit line shows the claim: press <b class="gd-ui">Credit them</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Not theirs</b>, with a reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A price typed by hand shows beside the rate-sheet price, with the reason. A price under the floor or past the discount limit is flagged: press <b class="gd-ui">Mark reviewed</b> once you have looked at it.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The renter has 48 hours to accept (and sign the amendment) or decline, with one reminder. Any extra is charged to their Card on File; a lower price raises a refund for your approval.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-review-requests" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review requests</h2><p class="gd-p">Every renter is asked for a review by email and text, as they chose, only from 9 am to 9 pm Toronto time. Nothing needs setting up.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Message</th><th scope="col">When</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mid-trip check-in</td><td>Rentals of 2 days or more, 24 hours after the pickup: &quot;How is the car? Reply or call if anything is off.&quot; No review ask.</td></tr><tr><td>Review request</td><td>1 hour after the check-in. It links the review page: the renter taps what they liked, adds a sentence, and gets a short draft to copy and post on Google.</td></tr><tr><td>Reminder</td><td>24 hours after the request.</td></tr><tr><td>Final follow-up</td><td>7 days after the request. Nothing more after it.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The booking page has the card Review requests: each message with when it went or when it will go, and why it stopped.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Ask for a review</b> sends the request now (or at 9 am if it is later than 9 pm), on any booking on a trip, returned or closed. Not twice in 24 hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On hold: a return or later charge (late return, kilometres, fuel, cleaning, smoking, damage, tolls and tickets) is not settled or waived, or an incident or dispute is open. The request goes by itself once they are. Press <b class="gd-ui">Send anyway</b> to send it now.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Mark reviewed</b> stops the messages when the renter tells you they already reviewed.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The messages also stop by themselves when the renter presses &quot;I already left a review&quot;, leaves a review on the site, unsubscribes, or a Google review is matched to them. <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Reviews</b> has the numbers (requests sent, on hold, reviews detected, the average rating), the hold list and the Google reviews to match.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The draft is made only from what the renter picked and wrote, and from the booking (the car, how long, delivery or pickup). Everyone gets the Google link, whatever their stars; a renter who gives 3 stars or fewer also sees &quot;Something wasn&#39;t right? Tell us directly&quot;.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-what-the-owner-sees-and-owner-deductions" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What the owner sees, and owner deductions</h2><p class="gd-p">Each booking on an owner&#39;s or partner&#39;s car shows the card What the owner sees at the top of its page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hide from the owner</b> keeps the booking&#39;s revenue from the owner until the car is returned, or until the owner statement covering it is approved. The owner sees the booking as Booked with its dates, and the calendar still shows the car busy. Add a reason if you like: it is kept in the history.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Show to the owner</b> shows it now. Approving the statement shows every hidden booking on it by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Not shown to the owner is for a booking with no owner revenue (an insurance placeholder, a shareholder&#39;s or the owner&#39;s own use at no charge): the owner sees only that the car is unavailable for those dates. A booking with revenue cannot be set this way.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add a rental and Send an offer have What the owner sees. It starts from Settings &gt; Program, Owners and fleet: Owners see a booking&#39;s revenue (right away by default).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">On the Money tab, Owner deductions on this booking: <b class="gd-ui">Add a booking expense</b> (cleaning, repair, fuel, platform fee or other, the amount, the reason the owner reads, a receipt number) comes off before Owner Revenue.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Set the Revenue Share for this booking</b> applies within the car&#39;s signed terms. Above the terms only an Admin can, with Above the signed terms ticked and the reason. <b class="gd-ui">Back to the car&#39;s terms</b> undoes it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Add a rental has the same under The car&#39;s owner.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The owner&#39;s statement always includes every booking at its true amounts and lists each deduction with its reason, so the payout is always right. Customer service and sales add deductions only while Program settings let them change fees.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'calendars', 'chapter', 'requests-offers-and-bookings', 'The master calendar shows every car, booking, request and block. Each car also has its own calendar and turnaround time.

## The master calendar

1. Move through time with the arrows and **Today**, or pick a date.
2. Choose the range: **Today**, **Week**, **2 weeks** or **Month**. **Agenda** shows a list instead.
3. The legend: confirmed, on rent, request, offer, not blocking, block and Turo.
4. Each row is a car. Bars are bookings and blocks; the red line is now.

![](/guides/img/admin-06-calendar-desktop-fed75400.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1000; address: carmacars.ca/admin/calendar; pins: 1 23.4 17.9, 2 45.3 17.9, 3 32.3 23.9, 4 66.6 33.0")

## Move a booking, add or remove a block

1. To move a booking, drag its bar to the new car or time, then press **Confirm the move**.
2. To block a car, double-click its row where the block starts, then press **Create the block**. **New block** at the top does the same.
3. To remove a block, open it and press **Remove the block**.

> Tip: After every confirmed trip a cleaning block holds the car for its turnaround time. It follows changes and extensions and goes away with a cancellation. Remove it from the side panel if the car is ready sooner; that time is then free.

## A car''s own calendar

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, then the car, then its Calendar tab.

1. The Calendar tab shows only this car, with its bookings and blocks.
2. Turnaround between trips on this car shows the time used. Press **Change** to give this car its own time.

![](/guides/img/admin-07-vehicle-calendar-desktop-98586ca8.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles/32d37609-00ed-4d39-ae12-9284421fb969?tab=calendar; pins: 1 42.1 31.1, 2 51.4 40.7")
', 'Calendars', 'The master calendar, moving bookings, blocks, cleaning time and a car''s calendar.',
  'The master calendar shows every car, booking, request and block. Each car also has its own calendar and turnaround time.

## The master calendar

1. Move through time with the arrows and **Today**, or pick a date.
2. Choose the range: **Today**, **Week**, **2 weeks** or **Month**. **Agenda** shows a list instead.
3. The legend: confirmed, on rent, request, offer, not blocking, block and Turo.
4. Each row is a car. Bars are bookings and blocks; the red line is now.

![](/guides/img/admin-06-calendar-desktop-fed75400.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1000; address: carmacars.ca/admin/calendar; pins: 1 23.6 20.0, 2 47.9 20.0, 3 38.9 31.4, 4 62.5 44.7")

## Move a booking, add or remove a block

1. To move a booking, drag its bar to the new car or time, then press **Confirm the move**.
2. To block a car, double-click its row where the block starts, then press **Create the block**. **New block** at the top does the same.
3. To remove a block, open it and press **Remove the block**.

> Tip: After every confirmed trip a cleaning block holds the car for its turnaround time. It follows changes and extensions and goes away with a cancellation. Remove it from the side panel if the car is ready sooner; that time is then free.

## A car''s own calendar

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, then the car, then its Calendar tab.

1. The Calendar tab shows only this car, with its bookings and blocks.
2. Turnaround between trips on this car shows the time used. Press **Change** to give this car its own time.

![](/guides/img/admin-07-vehicle-calendar-desktop-98586ca8.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles/b37ead6c-6196-4cd6-92ff-a14a55a8d5f2?tab=calendar; pins: 1 46.5 35.5, 2 50.1 46.2")
',
  '<p class="gd-p">The master calendar shows every car, booking, request and block. Each car also has its own calendar and turnaround time.</p><section class="gd-task" id="calendars-the-master-calendar" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The master calendar</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Move through time with the arrows and <b class="gd-ui">Today</b>, or pick a date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the range: <b class="gd-ui">Today</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Week</b>, <b class="gd-ui">2 weeks</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Month</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Agenda</b> shows a list instead.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The legend: confirmed, on rent, request, offer, not blocking, block and Turo.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Each row is a car. Bars are bookings and blocks; the red line is now.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/calendar</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1000"><img src="/guides/img/admin-06-calendar-desktop-fed75400.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1000"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:23.6%;top:20%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:47.9%;top:20%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:38.9%;top:31.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:62.5%;top:44.7%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="calendars-move-a-booking-add-or-remove-a-block" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Move a booking, add or remove a block</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">To move a booking, drag its bar to the new car or time, then press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm the move</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">To block a car, double-click its row where the block starts, then press <b class="gd-ui">Create the block</b>. <b class="gd-ui">New block</b> at the top does the same.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">To remove a block, open it and press <b class="gd-ui">Remove the block</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>After every confirmed trip a cleaning block holds the car for its turnaround time. It follows changes and extensions and goes away with a cancellation. Remove it from the side panel if the car is ready sooner; that time is then free.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="calendars-a-car-s-own-calendar" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car&#39;s own calendar</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, then the car, then its Calendar tab.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The Calendar tab shows only this car, with its bookings and blocks.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Turnaround between trips on this car shows the time used. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> to give this car its own time.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles/b37ead6c-6196-4cd6-92ff-a14a55a8d5f2?tab=calendar</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-07-vehicle-calendar-desktop-98586ca8.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:46.5%;top:35.5%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50.1%;top:46.2%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'fleet-and-listings', 'chapter', 'calendar-sync-with-turo-and-other-platforms', 'Vehicles is the fleet. Listings is the pipeline that turns a car into a page on carmacars.ca: photos, copy, a duplicate check and a covered plate on every public photo.

## Vehicles

**Cars** > **Vehicles**

1. Filter by status; More filters has who supplies the car, retired cars and the mode. Each row shows the plate, class, owner, mode, status, listing and daily rate.
2. Search by plate, model or owner. **Cars** > **Rates for many cars** changes the rates of many cars at once.
3. Open a car for its tabs: Overview, Rates, Fees and coverage, Calendar, Listing, and Owner, documents, tracker.

![](/guides/img/admin-08-vehicles-desktop-46461f49.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 900; address: carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles; pins: 1 18.5 19.3, 2 83.5 12.9, 3 73.6 38.9")

## Set a car''s rates and kilometres

Open the car, then the **Rates** tab. Everything on it saves together, in one step.

1. Type the four rates. Only the daily rate is needed: an empty weekend rate is the daily rate, an empty weekly rate is 6 days at the daily rate, and an empty monthly rate is 22 days.
2. Kilometres: keep **Use the defaults** (the kilometres a day in Settings, Kilometre choices, and the extra kilometre rate in Fee defaults for the car''s class), or choose **Custom for this car** and type them.
3. Check the deposit (the class default is filled in), and the delivery and pickup fees: each is one way, an empty pickup fee is the delivery fee, and 0 means not offered.
4. Read What renters pay under the fields: real prices for a weekend, a few weekdays, a week and a month, worked out the way bookings are priced. Press **Save the rates**.

| Rate | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Daily rate | A price per day, for each day that starts on a Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday |
| Weekend rate | A price per day, not for the whole weekend: each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday. Friday 10 am to Sunday 10 am is 2 days at this rate; Sunday to Monday is a daily day |
| Weekly rate | The price for 7 days. Rentals of 7 to 29 days cost this for each 7 days, counted by the day. A 1 to 6 day rental never costs more |
| Monthly rate | The price for 30 days. A 7 to 29 day rental never costs more |

> Tip: A problem shows on its own field, in words, as you type. When similar cars have rates, a line suggests them with Use these; it is only a hint. The same fields are on **Add a car**, so a car can be added with its rates in one pass.

> Coming soon: The Tracker card on a car says "Coming soon": live location, the remote immobilize request and mileage from the tracker need the tracker company''s connection first.

## The listing pipeline

Open **Cars** > **Listings**. A draft waiting for review shows Needs review.

1. Each row shows the car, plate, state, photos and the pipeline''s progress.
2. Press **Start a listing** to begin one for a car that has none.
3. Open a car to review it.

![](/guides/img/admin-09-listings-desktop-970819b6.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings; pins: 1 53.5 37.0, 2 87.2 21.1, 3 32.6 37.0")

## Review a listing

1. Pipeline shows each step done, such as photo sizes, copy draft and backgrounds.
2. Similar cars on file lists possible duplicates. Press **Not a duplicate** or **Same car**. An open flag does not keep the car off the site; only Same car does.
3. The copy is written by itself from the car''s facts and published when it passes the checks: nothing to type. To change a line, press Change; that field is then locked and kept by every new version.
4. Under Photos, each public photo shows its plate state: Plate not checked, Plate covered or No plate visible.

![](/guides/img/admin-10-listing-review-desktop-352745fd.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1100; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings/7e43d38d-32bb-4666-a742-81813c3b7671; pins: 1 20.6 16.6, 2 86.1 47.5, 3 19.9 106.8, 4 74.9 106.8")

## Cover the licence plate

On each public photo press **Cover the plate**. The editor opens.

1. The editor suggests a box over the plate. Check it. **Suggest the plate** asks again.
2. Drag over a plate to draw a box. Drag a box to move it, or its corner to resize it.
3. Under Cover the plate with, choose **A CarmaCars plate**, **Pixelation** or **Blur**.
4. Press **Save the covered photo**. **Clear the boxes** starts over.
5. No plate in the shot? Press **No plate visible on this photo**.

![](/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-desktop-4219ad93.jpg "desktop; size: 690 703; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings/7e43d38d-32bb-4666-a742-81813c3b7671; pins: 1 42.5 83.8, 2 49.6 29.9, 3 4.3 77.4, 4 15.5 83.8, 5 18.1 91.2")

> Tip: The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately. Keyboard: N adds a box, the arrows move it, Shift and the arrows resize it, Delete removes it.

## Publish

1. A real car that is not on the site is a line on To do: press **Set rates and publish**. The daily rate is filled in (the car''s own, or the suggested rate from similar cars or the class); change it if you like and press **Publish now**.
2. On the car itself, the Listing tab has **Publish now**; each open item of its checklist has a button to where it is done.
3. From a listing review: press **Approve and publish**, **Approve, publish later**, or **Send back** with what to fix.

> Watch out: The plate check never holds a car back: a real photo whose plate is not checked stays private (the other photos, or the sample photos, show instead) and goes public by itself once its plate is covered or marked not visible. Listings already live show "Plate not checked" on such photos.

## A listing without photos yet: sample photos

A car can be listed before its photos are taken. Until then the site shows a sample photo.

1. Submit the listing without photos. The listing copy is still written for you from the car''s details.
2. The car page and the car''s card show a sample photo, captioned "Sample photo", so renters know it is not this car. Staff see "Using sample photos" on the car and in Listings.
3. Publishing does not wait for a plate check: a sample photo has no plate.
4. Add the real photos when they are taken. Once real photos are approved they replace the sample at once; nothing else to do.

## Sample photos

**Settings** > **Sample photos**. The pictures a car shows until its real photos are in.

1. Every body type has a built-in picture (sedan, SUV, truck, van, coupe, hatchback, electric car).
2. Add your own: choose the Body type, and a Make and Model if the photo is of that exact model, pick the Photo, and press **Add the photo**.
3. The most specific photo wins: make and model, then make and body type, then body type. **Turn off** or **Delete** a photo you no longer want.
4. Cars using sample photos lists the cars still waiting for real photos. Each real car showing sample photos is also a line on To do, with **Add photos**.

![](/guides/img/admin-36-sample-photos-desktop-55c64070.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 812; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings/sample-photos; pins: 4 26.8 28.9")

## Publish now, and new cars published by themselves

Nothing between a new car and the site has to be finished first: the car goes on the site, and what is still open shows on its checklist.

1. **Settings** > **Program**, **Publish new cars automatically** (on by default): a new real car goes on the site by itself as soon as it has its year, make and model and its rates, when it is added with rates, when its rates are saved, when it is added for an owner, or when an owner''s application is approved.
2. Otherwise open the car: its Listing tab says why it is not on the site and has **Publish now**. A car with no rates yet is published with the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults in Program settings); change them later on the Rates tab.
3. Every real car has its listing from the moment it is added, as a draft. It shows in Listings and in Not on the site yet until it is published.
4. An owner''s own application waits for your decision before its car is published by itself; Publish now still works.
5. A car taken off the site by staff, or scheduled for a later date, is never published by itself: press **Publish now**.

## The checklist: what is still open on a listed car

Open items never stop publishing. They show as warnings on the car''s Listing tab and after Publish now.

| Item | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Paperwork | Ownership permit, registry forms, agreements signed, Forms C and D, upfront payment, registry visit, tracker, safety certificate |
| Insurance | Not on the fleet insurance policy yet: the car can be booked, but not handed over |
| Details | Colour, body, seats, gearbox: the car page leaves out what is missing |
| Photos | No real photos: sample photos stand in. A photo whose plate is not checked stays private until it is |
| No VIN yet | A car added by its plate alone: add the VIN when you have it |
| Possible duplicate | An open flag in Similar cars. Only Same car keeps the car off the site |
| Owner terms | The management fee (Revenue Share) and fees not set: a request uses the owner''s terms or the standard grid |

## The fleet policy rule at handover

A program owner''s car is listed and can be requested, offered and paid for while its paperwork is open. It is never handed over until the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet insurance policy.

- Staff see a warning on a request and an offer for a car not on the policy yet.
- The handover refuses the car until the insurer''s confirmation is recorded (Owners and onboarding). The field app says so on the job.
- Only real states keep a car off the site: retired, left the program, out of service, Turo only, bookings turned off, a self-managed owner in arrears, or a paused listing.
